  "text": {
    "paragraphs": [
      "Lily and Mia are at the beach. Grandma is with them. \"The sand is nice!\" says Mia. The sea is blue. The girls make sand cakes. One, two, three, four, five! Five cakes are on the sand. \"Our cakes are big,\" says Lily. Mia puts shells on the cakes.",
      "Then a big wave comes. The wave hits the five cakes. \"Oh no!\" says Lily. \"Our cakes!\" says Mia. The girls are sad. Grandma smiles. \"Let's make ten cakes,\" she says. \"Ten is a lot!\" says Mia. \"We can make them,\" says Grandma. One, two, three, four, five, six, seven, eight, nine, ten! Ten cakes are on the sand.",
      "Now it is lunch. Grandma has a bag. She has carrots and chips. \"How many chips are there?\" asks Lily. They count the chips. \"Eighteen chips,\" says Mia. \"Eighteen chips and six carrots,\" says Grandma. Lily and Mia eat the carrots. They eat the chips too. Our beach day is fun!"
    ],
